# adf-hx Browse POC — adf-hx Only

**Branch:** `feature/adf-hx-browse-poc`  
This rule applies to all work on the adf-hx browse POC. Do not mix production browse or generic Angular Material into this feature.

**Full architecture:** [`libs/shared/adf-hx-bridge/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../libs/shared/adf-hx-bridge/ARCHITECTURE.md)

## Architecture (summary)

```
Shell (nuxeo-ui)
  nav + drawer → BrowseAdfHxPocComponent  @  /#/browse-adf-hx?path=…
                      ↓ hxp-* components
                 adf-hx-bridge services (AdfHxDocumentService, …)
                      ↓ NuxeoDocumentApi / NuxeoQueryApi
                 nuxeo-client (BrowseService, DocumentDetailService)
                      ↓
                 Nuxeo REST
```

- **POC page:** `libs/features/browse/src/lib/browse-adf-hx-poc/` — wires tabs, filters, panel; no Material.
- **Bridge:** `libs/shared/adf-hx-bridge/` — all `hxp-*` UI + AdfHx services + Nuxeo→Hx mapper.
- **Production browse** (`/#/browse`) is unchanged; path sync and `browseReturn=adf-hx` helpers live in `browse-path.utils.ts`.
- **Scope A:** read-only — write actions show a notice; tabs/load/export are implemented.

## UI — real adf-hx components first, `hxp-*` for what adf-hx lacks

**This section was rewritten in Phase 3. Its previous form banned Angular Material outright, which
was correct while every component here was hand-written and is wrong now: five real adf-hx
components are adopted and adf-core brings Material in transitively. An agent following the old rule
would try to remove working code.** `docs/adf-hx-beta-plan.md` lists updating it as a hard rule for
this phase.

- **Prefer the real upstream component.** `HxpDocumentListComponent`, `HxpBreadcrumbComponent`,
  `HxpDocumentTreeComponent`, `ManageVersionsSidebarComponent` and `HxpPropertiesSidebarComponent`
  are adopted from `@alfresco/adf-hx-content-services/ui`, and each replaced a hand-written
  equivalent that was deleted in the same change. Do not reintroduce a local imitation of a
  component upstream provides.
- **Material arrives transitively through adf-core, and that is expected.** The adopted panels
  render `mat-select`, `mat-expansion-panel`, `mat-icon-button` and Material form fields. Do not
  strip it.
- **Still do not reach for Material *directly* in our own `hxp-*` components.** Those exist for
  what adf-hx does not provide — see `docs/adf-hx-workarounds.md` category 2 — and they stay native
  HTML styled in bridge SCSS so they carry no Material dependency of their own. `hxp-icon`,
  `hxp-spinner`, `hxp-column-picker`, `hxp-document-cards`, `hxp-browse-toolbar` and
  `hxp-browse-pager` all follow this.
- **Never** use Satori (`sat-*`) or production browse UI in the POC page or its bridge components.
- Side nav: `hxp-browse-nav-drawer`, which now hosts upstream's `HxpDocumentTreeComponent`. The
  hand-written `hxp-browse-nav-tree` was deleted when the real tree was adopted.
- CSS tokens: prefer **`--hxp-*`** in bridge SCSS, aliased from Satori in
  `apps/nuxeo-ui/src/styles/hxp-theme.scss`. `--mat-sys-*` with a literal fallback is acceptable
  where a component sits inside adf-core markup, which is why `hxp-browse-pager` uses it.
- Overriding an adopted component's styles needs `::ng-deep`, because upstream ships
  `ViewEncapsulation.None`. Register it — see category 1, W9.

## Data — AdfHx bridge only

- Feature page and nav tree must call **`AdfHxDocumentService`** (and other bridge services), not `BrowseService` or `DocumentDetailService` directly.
- Document model: **`Document`** from `@hylandsoftware/hxcs-js-client`.
- Routing/navigation: **`NuxeoDocumentRouterService`** + `AdfHxBrowseContextService`.
- Providers: `ADF_HX_NUXEO_BRIDGE_PROVIDERS` on the feature page and nav drawer.

## Shell integration

- App shell may host `<hxp-browse-nav-drawer>` but must **not** render Material chrome (title/refresh) for adf-hx browse — the drawer component owns its header.
- Do not import production `BrowseComponent` patterns into the POC route.

## PR blocker

Any new Material, Satori, direct `BrowseService` usage, or production browse component in the above paths must be removed before merge.
